{:measured "2026-09-30"
 :postgres-ref "REL_17_7"
 ;; Per-file agreement: the share of PostgreSQL's expected output
 ;; lines that appear, in order, in ours. `bb pg-regress-gate`
 ;; fails when a file drops more than the tolerance below, when an
 ;; exact match is lost, or when a file stops being measurable.
 ;;
 ;; The tolerance is not slack for regressions: a file that is
 ;; mostly cascade realigns by a point or two whenever anything
 ;; ahead of its first divergence changes, in either direction.
 ;;
 ;; And the number is GAMEABLE: it counts expected lines we
 ;; reproduce, so emitting MORE output can only raise it. A
 ;; wrong-but-plausible block of rows scores above a clean
 ;; refusal. Read a file's score to decide what to open next,
 ;; never as a goal. See `agreement`.
 :tolerance 3.0
